WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.100
So I'm going to make a prediction.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.640
The chances of this video going viral is this
big.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.640
Here's why.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.700
Because no one cares to talk about customer
complaints.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:15.110
But I promise you, I want to challenge you
to listen to this whole thing because it will

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.230
save you a lot of sleepless nights, it will
make you a lot of money, it will save you

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.900
a lot of money and it will just create a culture
for your company.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.929
So let's get right into it.

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:25.109
Complaints are a part of business.

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:31.220
When you decide to become a business owner,
you are putting yourself out there for customers

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:38.080
to say you are not as good as XYZ and it is
our job to hear them out and get better because

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.020
this is free counsel that people are giving
you.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.020
Just think about it.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:48.640
There's companies that do focus groups that
pay $75 per participant to just show up and

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.610
complain about your product and you're getting
all these things for free.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.290
That's one of the things I want you to be
keeping in mind.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.930
Now let's talk about how I look at complaints.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.620
There are five different types of complainers
when it comes down to your business and no

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.340
matter what you do, there's five different
types of people that complain about what you

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.340
do.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.359
The number one type of complainer is the valid
complaint.

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:10.570
This is the person that's right.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.840
You did something wrong.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.009
Your company didn't do the right thing.

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:18.310
The procedures, the offers, anything that
happened, they're absolutely right with what

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.310
took place.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.909
And I'm going to explain you how to handle
that.

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:24.170
But the first one is the valid complainers.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.090
Whatever complaint that was made, you have
to figure out how to improve that.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.490
The pessimist.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:33.429
This is the person that no matter where you
go with them, nothing can ever make them happy.

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:34.689
Nothing can make them happy.

00:01:34.689 --> 00:01:40.660
So you can do anything and everything for
them, they will never be happy with what you

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.660
do for them.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.020
This is the customer you have as well.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.490
The third type of customer is the one that
they like your product, they disagree with

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.490
your beliefs.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:55.560
For instance, hypothetically, imagine the
CEO of Starbucks gets up and he says, "I believe

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.939
that healthcare should be free for everybody."

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:03.609
And there's someone that goes to Starbucks
and loves the coffee, but they absolutely

00:02:03.609 --> 00:02:08.860
disagree politically with what Howard Schultz
believes when it comes down to national healthcare.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:16.010
For example, imagine if you are the CEO of
Wal-Mart, and you believe in capitalism, and

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:21.239
they always go to Wal-Mart and shop, but they
HATE what the company stands for and they

00:02:21.239 --> 00:02:25.819
support certain people politically or a team
or whatever it is, so they have a vendetta

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:26.819
toward you.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:27.819
I'll give you a story.

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:31.319
One time with a rant complainer that happened
with me.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:36.810
This was six and a half years ago, we had
just started our firm, and I will never forget

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.360
what happened with this story here because
I remember I got this, all of a sudden, this

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:46.440
person started posting all over our Facebook,
Twitter, you know, every single website that

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.659
we had, they were just complaining, complaining,
complaining, this company sucks, this CEO's

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:52.829
horrible, bop, bop, bop, bop, all this stuff.

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:56.370
So finally, I called Mario, and I said, "Mario,
I need to get that guy's number.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.370
I'm going to call him."

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.830
So I get his number.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.500
I call him up, at night.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.870
I'll never forget it.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.269
It's 10:00 at night.

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:06.730
It's 8:00 his time, I'm on the phone with
him.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.980
I said, "Hey, this is Patrick Bet-David, giving
you a, The CEO of PHP.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.230
I just wanted to call you.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.180
It seems you're extremely upset.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.950
I wanted to call you instead of having someone
else call you.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.000
Can you tell me what you're not happy about?"

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.450
And we went on a 45-minute conversation.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.780
Do you want to know what this conversation
was over?

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.689
Let me tell you what this conversation was
over.

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:32.829
This conversation was over the fact that he
belonged to the biggest communistic organization

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:38.790
in America and he's a proud believer and follower
of Karl Marx, a book called Communist Manifesto.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.859
And he found out that I believe in capitalism
and I followed the teaching of Milton Freedman,

00:03:43.859 --> 00:03:45.780
and he HATES capitalism.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.030
He hates capitalism!

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.970
So I'll never forget the conversation that
we had together and this became a friendly

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:52.970
conversation.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.010
So I said, "Why do you hate capitalism?"

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:57.290
And he said, "I hate capitalism because all
they care about is they put the people to

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.290
work."

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.519
And I said, okay, let's take capitalism out.

00:03:59.519 --> 00:04:00.829
Where do you work at right now?

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:02.470
He said, "I know where you're going with this."

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.470
Where do you work at?

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.760
He said, "I work at PF Changs."

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.499
I said, "What happens if PF Changs goes out
of business?"

00:04:06.499 --> 00:04:08.249
He said, I'll go work for another company.

00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:09.519
I don't care about PF Changs."

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:13.120
I said, "You're going to go work for another
capitalist.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.540
What if that capitalist goes out of business?"

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.769
I'm going to go get another job, because I
will always be needed.

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:20.120
I said, "Without the capitalists, you don't
have a job.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.069
So we had this friendly debate.

00:04:22.069 --> 00:04:26.610
Fast forward six years later, literally nine
months ago, this guy sends me a message saying,

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.000
you don't remember me.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.000
Of course I remember him.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.610
I have a pretty decent memory.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:36.139
You won't remember me, but we debated six
years ago when I was a communist and I just

00:04:36.139 --> 00:04:39.560
want you to know I follow every single Valuetainment
video, and I believe in capitalism.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:40.560
Things have changed.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.560
I'm 29 years old.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.630
Back then I was 23 years old.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.770
I said, okay, no problem.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.720
But I had to figure out that that person had
no problem with our product.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.310
They had a problem with the belief system
and although I can't change that, I heard

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.260
him out, we fixed it, we moved on from there.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.180
The fourth type of complainers that you have
that's become a very big business is an actual

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.220
enemy.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:03.140
So what I mean by an enemy or a competitor,
this has become a very, very big business.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.490
Let me explain.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:10.240
So here's a big gorilla, big guy, big company
that's been doing a business and you're planning

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.310
on coming and taking a percentage of their
business away from them, right?

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.310
You're an enemy.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.310
You're a threat.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.310
They don't like you.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.590
You need to go out of business ASAP.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:21.450
And so we started a company, and we're trying
to take distribution away from some folks.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:25.259
When I say distribution, the amount of life
insurance that's being written, so we want

00:05:25.259 --> 00:05:27.190
to start writing this business.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.770
That didn't make a lot of people happy.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.240
That ticked off a lot of people.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:36.250
So all of a sudden, we got a floodgate, we
got flooded with negative complaints online.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:40.449
And you could tell, there was a lot of things
being said that's inaccurate with details,

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:44.250
where you know somebody else was doing it
and eventually we went and investigated it

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.090
and we realized what's going on with that.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.401
And there's nothing we could do about it.

00:05:47.401 --> 00:05:48.820
Here's why there's nothing we could do about
it.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.210
Because companies like Yelp, as much as I
use Yelp as a customer to go figure out what

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:59.970
restaurants are out there and which restaurant
to choose around the world, I don't like what

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.590
Yelp does to small business owners.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.020
I'll tell you exactly what Yelp does to small
business owners.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:08.979
yelp will come up to you and they'll say,
"If you advertise $6,000 a month, $5,000 a

00:06:08.979 --> 00:06:14.979
month, we will give you a shot at putting
out more positive reviews and all this other

00:06:14.979 --> 00:06:15.979
stuff.

00:06:15.979 --> 00:06:17.410
When they went public, they changed their
script.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.569
I'll never forget it because I spoke to one
of their reps.

00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:21.949
He said, Patrick, yes, we used to do that.

00:06:21.949 --> 00:06:26.129
But we don't do that anymore because now we're
public and we have so many different people

00:06:26.129 --> 00:06:30.430
that have said that we did that and now we
have to answer to that so all this stuff he

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:31.430
started telling me.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:35.449
So I said the reality part of it is after
some employees left Yelp, they started telling

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:38.349
us that this is what they're doing and that's
a business nowadays.

00:06:38.349 --> 00:06:43.351
They take small businesses that are frightened
to go out of business and through fear, because

00:06:43.351 --> 00:06:46.360
of a small restaurant being a three-star people
will not go.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.849
Their business drops by 20%, they ask you
for $6000 a month.

00:06:49.849 --> 00:06:55.060
So it's a legal, online Mafia type of thing
if you want to call it like back in the days,

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.740
you know how people would come and say, hey,
you got to pay me more taxes if you want to

00:06:58.740 --> 00:06:59.740
do business.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:00.740
It's something like that going on.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.210
You got to figure out a way to work around
that.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:06.040
The reason you have to figure out a way to
work around that is because eventually when

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:09.479
you earn saint status, none of that stuff
matters.

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:14.409
And saint status takes about a decade, five
years to ten years depending on the business

00:07:14.409 --> 00:07:15.849
that you have to earn.

00:07:15.849 --> 00:07:22.330
And once you earn saint status, this means
when your positive experiences are just crushing

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:26.770
the negative comments that no one even pays
attention to the negative comments any more.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.669
You don't even think about Apple's negative
comments.

00:07:28.669 --> 00:07:31.000
You know how many negative comments Apple
gets.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.000
People still go to Apple.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.669
You don't even care about Wal-Mart's negative
complaints any more.

00:07:34.669 --> 00:07:36.229
You know how many people work at Wal-Mart.

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:38.940
2.3 million people, 1.4 million in America.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:43.669
I just got the update because last week I
said 1.5 million, 2.2, it's 1.4 million in

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:49.189
America, 2.3 million around the world, 900,000
people around the world work for Wal-Mart,

00:07:49.189 --> 00:07:53.479
even though they have more complaints than
almost any other company in the world, they

00:07:53.479 --> 00:07:56.610
also happen to be the biggest company in the
world, top three biggest companies in the

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.610
world depending on the time.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.259
Then the fifth one is the final one is the
trolls.

00:08:00.259 --> 00:08:01.470
Nowadays there's trolls.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:05.289
Trolls has become a new thing, because this
is a way for someone to get fame.

00:08:05.289 --> 00:08:09.270
This is a way for someone to say oh my gosh,
I'm going to go mess with this company because

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.729
I may get publicity and I may get picked up.

00:08:11.729 --> 00:08:12.729
So it's become a business.

00:08:12.729 --> 00:08:16.689
There's actually, you can go to sites that
tell you how to be a professional troller.

00:08:16.689 --> 00:08:17.689
It's hilarious.

00:08:17.689 --> 00:08:21.169
We get some trolls sometimes on Valuetainment.

00:08:21.169 --> 00:08:23.000
I had this one guy that trolled me one time.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.599
I won't tell you what I told him, but he trolled
me.

00:08:25.599 --> 00:08:30.000
Paul is already laughing back there because,
so this guy comes in, he starts trolling Valuetainment.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.530
And then I go to his Facebook page, and on
his Facebook Page, the most recent post he

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:38.079
posted, he said, "I'm in the mood to go troll
some bigger brands."

00:08:38.079 --> 00:08:39.079
This is on his Facebook Page!

00:08:39.079 --> 00:08:42.419
So I took a screenshot and I said, "Let's
have some fun."

00:08:42.419 --> 00:08:44.950
Because if you want to have fun, I don't mind
it.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.089
Crap talking games.

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:47.790
I went at him pretty hard.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.970
He deleted his comment and came back.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.070
We had a fun time with it.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:55.941
But trolls, I appreciate trolls because at
least they're trying to become celebrities.

00:08:55.941 --> 00:08:58.070
So don't take trolls too seriously.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.450
They're actually fun to be dealing with.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.329
So you have those five types of complainers.

00:09:01.329 --> 00:09:05.790
Now let's talk about your business and how
to handle these complaints.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:10.589
First of all, depending on the type of a business
you run, your volume of sales that come in

00:09:10.589 --> 00:09:15.130
will dictate how many opportunities there
are for people to complain with your product,

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:20.370
meaning if your volume of sales is high, there's
more likelihood of you having complaints.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:28.600
So for example, if I take 1,000 shots in a
basketball game, vs. another guy that comes

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:33.890
in and only gets one shot in a basketball
game, who has the higher likelihood of shooting

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:35.019
an air ball?

00:09:35.019 --> 00:09:39.080
The guy that shoots 1,000 shots, or the guy
that shoots one shot? 1,000 shots is going

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.670
to get some air balls.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:44.000
And air balls could be complaints, it could
be a misplay, it could be something that happened

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.000
that you have to address.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.090
So you've got to understand the business you've
chosen to be a part of.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.940
And if it's high volume, you're going to get
more complaints.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:54.930
Low volume, fewer complaints, and so it's
simply on the way you do your business.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:56.980
So now how you handle complains when you get
them.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.060
It's very simple.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.450
#1: the most important thing before I tell
you how to respond is the following.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.450
Speed is your game.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.450
Speed.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.470
The complaint happens Tuesday.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.459
If you get back to them by Friday, it's already
too late.

00:10:07.459 --> 00:10:12.639
Complaint happens at Tuesday, at 3:00 in the
afternoon, if you have a system where you

00:10:12.639 --> 00:10:15.980
get back to them within a day, that's better
than Friday.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:19.170
But if you have a way to get back to them
immediately, because you get prompted with

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:23.560
a notification that somebody's not happy,
you get back to them within an hour, that

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:24.750
means it matters to them.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.630
So speed is your number one game of handling
complaints.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:31.100
#2 when it comes down to handling complaints
is avoiding conflict.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:36.250
If you avoid conflict, I guarantee you, you
will constantly be getting complaints.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:41.450
So let me tell you what type of brands I am
extremely suspicious of.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:46.279
I remember one time I sat down with a guy
and he said, "I turned off all my comments

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:47.279
on YouTube."

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:52.300
I said, "Why?" he said, "Well, you know YouTube
has a way for you to hide your number of subscribers

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:55.980
and hide your number of comments because no
one will know how many subscribers you have

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.000
so you can kind of make it up and say how
many you have, and no one will say the bad

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.220
things people are saying about you."

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:04.420
I said, "First of all, I want to hear the
negative comments because I want to figure

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.411
out a way for sound is not good.

00:11:06.411 --> 00:11:10.540
You know how many things we've improved on
our brand because of how many Valuetainers

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.570
have told us the sound only comes from one
ear.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:15.810
Paul, how many times have you gotten a message
where [Paul: Too many!].

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:20.110
Too many times, so Paul over here, he's got
to figure that part out.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.360
Or hey, you guys spelled Entrepreneur wrong.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:28.200
We chose this word called entrepreneur and
every time entre pre pre neur, pre neur, Paul,

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.899
pre neur, right?

00:11:29.899 --> 00:11:32.260
So, hey, you misspelled entrepreneur.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:33.260
Great.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.800
We want to hear this stuff.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.880
Brands that are too concerned about hiding
all the negative comments, I'm very suspicious

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.880
about.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:40.959
What are you hiding?

00:11:40.959 --> 00:11:42.060
Who cares about negative comments?

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.060
No one's perfect.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.040
See, we don't have a standard of perfection.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.140
I want to hear about it.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:50.610
Because I want to see what my audience is
going to say about it so we can be held accountable

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:51.700
and we can improve.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:55.310
